    """Recover source for a single language target as a typed ``CanonicalSource``.

    Wired language families and the pass that backs each:
    ``python``/``pyc`` (py-decompile), ``jvm-class``/``class``/``java`` and
    ``kotlin`` (jvm lifter), ``lua`` (register lifter), ``ruby`` (YARV/mruby
    recovery), ``php``/``php-bytecode`` (eval-chain peel / op-array skeleton),
    and ``javascript``/``js``/``typescript``/``ts`` (unminify). Binary-only
    targets (``go``, ``swift``, ``wasm``) have no single recovered-source body;
    call their structural binding (``go_analyze``, ``swift_analyze``,
    ``wasm_analyze``) or ``parse`` instead.
    """
    ...

def disasm(language: str, source: str | bytes) -> str:
    """Render a bytecode/instruction listing as text.

    Wired: ``python``/``pyc``, ``jvm-class``/``class``, ``dex``, ``beam``,
    ``hermes``, ``wasm``, ``ruby``/``yarv``/``mruby`` (YARV disassembly or mruby
    irep summary), and ``php``/``php-bytecode`` (Zend op-array listing). Lua
    recovery is lifter-based; use ``decompile('lua', ...)`` or
    ``parse('lua', ...)`` instead of a raw listing.
    """
    ...

